NCMAT v5
#
# Nickel oxide NiO (bunsenite), rock-salt structure (space group 225), for the twin of ODIN (exercise "Where has the
# fuel-cell anode been reduced?"). Not in the standard library of NCrystal: written for the twin.
#
# Lattice parameter at room temperature a = 4.177 A (e.g. COD 1010093; the Bragg edges NiO(200) at 4.17 A and
# NiO(220) at 2.95 A measured by Makowska et al., ECS Trans. 68, 1103 (2015), give a = 4.17 A).
# Lattice dynamics: Debye model, Debye temperature 500 K for both elements (assumed: values of 400 to 600 K are
# reported for NiO). Its antiferromagnetic order (magnetic Bragg peaks, the first at d = 4.82 A, edge at 9.6 A, outside
# the band of the exercise) is not modeled: NCrystal treats nuclear scattering only.
#
@CELL
  cubic 4.177
@SPACEGROUP
  225
@ATOMPOSITIONS
  Ni 0   0   0
  Ni 0   1/2 1/2
  Ni 1/2 0   1/2
  Ni 1/2 1/2 0
  O  1/2 0   0
  O  0   1/2 0
  O  0   0   1/2
  O  1/2 1/2 1/2
@DYNINFO
  element  Ni
  fraction 1/2
  type     vdosdebye
  debye_temp 500
@DYNINFO
  element  O
  fraction 1/2
  type     vdosdebye
  debye_temp 500
